{
  "_why": "Controls the clicking sweep never acts on, each with the reason. Anything not here and not clicked is reported as a facet nobody has thought about. Being in this file is a decision somebody can disagree with; being in neither state is not an answer.",
  "Finish.button:Finish_SendNow": "Sends real incidents to the live importer under the agency's ORI. It is not a rehearsal, and a sweep that runs every night must not upload every night. Covered instead by the Handover sweep, which uploads a batch with no incidents in it against a stub.",
  "Finish.button:Elevate": "Restarts the application with administrator rights, which ends the process the walk is driving. The elevated restart is covered by ElevatedRestartTests against a seam.",
  "Finish.button:Restart": "The other half of the elevated restart, and the same reason: it replaces the process mid-walk.",
  "Exit.button:Exit_CloseAnyway": "Closes the application. Pressing it would end the walk at whatever point it was reached, and what it does is covered by ExitModel's own tests.",
  "Index.button:Login_Forget": "Forgets the stored upload key. The key is the one credential this machine has for the test ORI, and a sweep that discards it leaves every later run unable to sign in.",
  "FileSource.button:Browse": "Opens the operating system's file dialog, which is a native window the page cannot dismiss. The walk would stop there until somebody closed it by hand.",
  "OdbcQuery.button:Odbc_Analyse": "Reads the whole schema and can take a minute on a real database. It is walked deliberately by the query-screen journey rather than pressed in passing.",
  "Finish.button:Automation_CloseToTray": "Parks the window and closes it, which ends every journey that follows. Pressed on purpose by the tray journey, at the end, where it is the thing being tested.",
  "Automation.button:Automation_CloseToTray": "Parks the window and closes it, which ends every journey that follows -- the same reason as its twin on the Finish screen, which was declared while this one was not. Measured: the walk pressed it here, the application went to the notification area, and every screen after it answered connection refused. Pressed on purpose by the tray journey, at the end, where it is the thing being tested.",
  "Automation.tick:AllAgencies": "Offered only when the setup holds more than one agency THAT COULD ACTUALLY UPLOAD -- the batch screen lists an agency only once its upload key is in Credential Manager, because a batch file for an agency with no key runs and sends nothing. A sweep has one test ORI and one key, and storing keys for agencies that do not exist is the one thing it must never do. The split itself is walked: the agency grid, its ORIs and its ticks are all clicked on the agencies screen.",
  "Automation.tick:Chosen": "The same gate as Automation.tick:AllAgencies -- one row per agency with a stored upload key, and a sweep has exactly one.",
  "Classify.button:use-format": "Appears only when the detector is unsure of a date column and offers a format to accept. The test database returns real DATE columns, which are never ambiguous, so nothing is ever suggested. Reaching it would mean shipping a fixture whose dates are text in an odd shape, and the rule it would prove -- that accepting a suggestion assigns that format -- is held by the classification tests.",
  "OdbcQuery.button:Odbc_AddJoin": "The join grid exists only after the schema has been read AND a table chosen, and adding a join needs both to survive every other press on that screen. The walk reads the schema and chooses a table -- the table button, the join rows, their kind, their table and the button that removes one are all clicked -- but the Add button sits behind a form the walk's own presses keep replacing. Named debt, not a decision.",
  "OdbcQuery.button:Odbc_PreviewButton": "Shows the first few rows of a chosen table. Same gate as the join grid: it needs a table selection that survives the presses around it. Named debt.",
  "OdbcQuery.button:Odbc_SqlTakeBack": "Offered by the designer only once it has noticed the statement was edited by hand, and only while that is still true -- the walk rewrites the box on every round, which puts the designer back in charge before the button can be pressed. What it does is held by the designer's own tests. Named debt.",
  "FileSource.button:File_Load": "There is no read-the-file button on that screen, deliberately: choosing a file is the whole instruction, and a path typed into the box is read the moment it is finished with. What the census sees is a submit marked visually-hidden, tabindex=-1 and aria-hidden, which exists so that pressing Enter in the box submits the form. Nobody can click it, including a screen reader -- and that is the point of it."
}
